witter:image:alt" content="Rumman, ERP inteligente guiado para Android"><meta name="theme-color" content="#FCF9FD" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)"><meta name="theme-color" content="#17121F" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any"><link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/fonts/sora-latin-variable.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/fonts/inter-latin-variable.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css?v=20260728-1"><script src="/assets/theme-init.js?v=20260728-1"></script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage","name":"Rumman Privacy Policy","dateModified":"2026-07-28"}</script></head><body><a class="skip-link" href="#conteudo">Skip to content</a><header class="topbar"><nav class="nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="Rumman — home"><span class="brand-icon"><img src="/assets/icon-192.png" width="192" height="192" alt=""></span><span class="brand-name">Rumman</span></a><div class="nav-panel" id="primary-navigation" data-menu-panel data-open="false"><div class="nav-links"><a class="nav-link" href="/en/">Home</a><a class="nav-link" href="/en/features">Features</a><a class="nav-link" href="/en/how-it-works">How it works</a><a class="nav-link" href="/en/how-to-use">How to use</a><a class="nav-link" href="/en/use-cases">Use cases</a><a class="nav-link" href="/en/plans">Plans</a><a class="nav-link" href="/en/faq">FAQ</a><a class="nav-link" href="/en/blog/">Blog</a></div><a class="nav-cta" href="/en/plans">Discover Rumman</a></div><div class="nav-controls"><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle data-label-light="Use light theme" data-label-dark="Use dark theme" aria-label="Use dark theme" title="Use dark theme"><span aria-hidden="true">☾</span></button><button class="menu-toggle" type="button" data-menu-toggle aria-controls="primary-navigation" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Open menu"><span></span><span></span><span></span></button></div></nav></header><main id="conteudo"><article class="legal-page"><header class="legal-header"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Rumman · ERP Android</p><h1>Rumman Privacy Policy</h1><p class="hero-lead">How Rumman handles local data, synchronized records, account security, diagnostics, backup and Assistant requests.</p><p class="legal-updated">Effective and last updated: 26 July 2026.</p></div></header><div class="wrap legal-content"><section><h2>1. Local-first architecture</h2><p>The operational database remains primarily in the app private storage, and routines that do not require internet continue to work locally.</p><p>When a verified account uses a team or synchronization between devices, structured business records are also synchronized with the company workspace. Credentials, tokens, local paths, item photos and external files are excluded from that payload.</p></section><section><h2>2. Cloud processing</h2><p>Firebase processes account, authentication, integrity and diagnostic data. Cloudflare processes workspace members, roles, invitations, versions, structured ERP records and Assistant requests initiated by the user.</p></section><section><h2>3. Backup and export</h2><p>Android may copy the operational database to the private area of the user Google Account when device backup is enabled. The user may also create a password-protected .rumman file and save it through the Android file picker. Rumman does not store or recover that password.</p></section><section><h2>4. AI Assistant</h2><p>Content is sent only after the user confirms the request. The gateway does not store prompts or responses in D1, and sensitive information that is not necessary should not be submitted.</p></section><section><h2>5. Purposes and permissions</h2><p>Data is used to protect the account, maintain the workspace, synchronize authorized devices, apply roles and limits, diagnose failures, prevent abuse and deliver requested features. The camera is used only for chosen scans and images.</p></section><section><h2>6. Providers and security</h2><p>Google Firebase, Google Play Integrity and Cloudflare provide infrastructure. Data may be processed outside Brazil under applicable safeguards. Traffic uses HTTPS. Rumman does not sell data or display ads.</p></section><section><h2>7. Retention, deletion and rights</h2><p>Local data remains until the user deletes it, clears Android app data or uninstalls Rumman. Remote account and workspace data is removed when account deletion is completed, subject to legal and security retention requirements.</p><p>For access, correction, portability where applicable or deletion, use the app privacy area, visit the public deletion page or contact e-mail@rumman.app.br.</p></section><section><h2>8. Children, changes and contact</h2><p>Rumman is a business management product and is not directed to children. Relevant changes will be communicated in the app or on this page. Public support and privacy contact: e-mail@rumman.app.br.</p></section></div></article></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="wrap footer-main"><div class="footer-brand-block"><a class="brand footer-brand" href="/en/"><span class="brand-icon"><img src="/assets/icon-192.png" width="192" height="192" alt=""></span><span class="brand-name">Rumman</span></a><p>Guided intelligent Android ERP for small businesses.</p><a class="footer-contact" href="mailto:e-mail@rumman.app.br">Contact Rumman: e-mail@rumman.app.br</a><nav class="language-switcher footer-language" aria-label="Language"><span class="visually-hidden">Language</span><a href="/privacidade" lang="pt-BR">PT</a><a href="/en/privacy" lang="en" aria-current="page">EN</a><a href="/es/privacidad" lang="es">ES</a><a href="/fr/confidentialite" lang="fr">FR</a></nav></div><div class="footer-links"><strong>Product</strong><a href="/en/features">Featur